# PRODUCTION ENHANCEMENT PROMPT — Add 20 Professional Website Features to My Restaurant SaaS

## Your mission

Act as a senior full-stack engineer, UI/UX designer, accessibility specialist, and QA engineer working directly inside my existing Google AI Studio project.

Upgrade my existing AI-powered restaurant management SaaS by implementing the 20 features specified below.

**This is an implementation task, not a design exercise.** Inspect the existing application, identify the correct files and components, implement the features fully, run tests, resolve defects, and verify the finished behavior.

Do not create a new unrelated application, replace the existing architecture unnecessarily, or damage existing functionality.

Preserve the current database, Firebase integration, authentication, restaurant workspaces, inventory, purchasing, customers, reviews, tips, staff management, AI assistant, subscription plans, payment integrations, and administrative features.

Use the existing frameworks and design system wherever possible. Make additional dependencies only when they provide a clear benefit.

## 1. Dark mode toggle

Implement a fully functional dark mode and light mode toggle.

Requirements:
- Provide a visible theme switch in the main navigation or user settings.
- Apply the theme consistently to the public website, authenticated dashboards, forms, tables, dialogs, menus, charts, and notifications.
- Persist the selected preference between visits.
- Respect the operating system's theme on the first visit when no preference has been saved.
- Avoid flashes of the wrong theme during page loading.
- Ensure readable text, accessible contrast, visible form states, and appropriate borders in both themes.
- Do not hardcode theme colors independently across every component; use shared design tokens or CSS variables.
- Ensure charts, icons, and status indicators remain distinguishable in both themes.

Acceptance test: changing the theme updates the whole interface, survives a refresh, and does not reset during normal navigation.

## 2. Professional announcement banner

Create a reusable announcement banner for the public website and, when appropriate, the authenticated dashboard.

Use cases include new features, service announcements, maintenance notices, new subscription offers, and restaurant-specific announcements.

Requirements:
- Support configurable text, optional links, severity or announcement type, and an optional dismiss action.
- Allow authorized administrators to create, edit, publish, and disable platform announcements.
- Allow restaurant owners to configure announcements for their own restaurant website if website customization supports it.
- Avoid showing expired, unpublished, or unauthorized announcements.
- Persist dismissals appropriately and respect the configured announcement lifetime.
- Ensure announcements never cover critical navigation or payment controls.
- Display correctly on mobile and desktop.

Do not invent discounts or claim a new service exists when it has not been configured.

